SM(297,{"n":"Exodus 19","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Exodus 19.mp3","d":2990.4,"s":[[0.24,"Come and study the Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.96,"Father Stephen holds a PhD in biblical studies, and it's an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[21.6,"Okay, chapter 19."],[23.76,"So in the third month after the children of Israel departed from the land of Egypt, on the same day, they came into the Sinai Desert."],[33.36,"For they departed from Rephidim, came into the Sinai Desert, and camped in the desert."],[39.44,"So Israel camped there before the mountain."],[43.52,"So they they've now gotten to Sinai, they're now camped at the base of the mountain."],[51.76,"Then Moses went up to the mountain of God, and God called to him from the mountain, saying, Thus you shall say to the house of Jacob, and tell the children of Israel, you have seen what I did to the Egyptians, and how I bore you on eagle's wings and brought you to myself."],[68.28,"Now let me be clear."],[69.64,"This is not literal."],[72.84,"This is not Lord of the Rings."],[76.92,"Eagles did not come and pick them up and carry them out."],[81.0,"That's not what this is saying."],[82.2,"This may be where Tolkien got the idea."],[84.68,"You have to ask Father Andrew."],[86.68,"You can email him at fatherandrew at ancient faith.com."],[92.04,"And ask him about that, but uh this is obviously figurative language."],[99.64,"Now, therefore, if you will indeed obey my voice and keep my covenant, you shall be a special people. to me above all nations, for all the earth is mine"],[109.12,"You shall be to me a royal priesthood and a holy nation."],[112.56,"These are the words you shall speak to the children of Israel."],[115.84,"Okay, so a few things here."],[118.0,"First, I have, as we've been going through Genesis and Exodus, given you the beginnings of a small list of things that do not interest me."],[127.44,"You may remember one of those was the age of the earth."],[130.56,"You may remember one of those was the date of the Exodus."],[133.12,"Well, here's a third one: the location of Mount Sinai."],[137.04,"Um. Endless journal articles."],[141.12,"Endless stuff. But we need to notice something."],[145.04,"Need to notice something."],[148.6,"Because we've been hearing about the mountain of God as we've been going through Exodus."],[155.96,"When we first heard about the mountain of God, it was the mountain that Moses went to while he was tending his father-in-law's herds."],[166.97,"In that area where Jethro lived."],[171.45,"That was a mountain of God."],[173.45,"Then he said, We're gonna take Israel to the mountain of God."],[176.25,"Now they've come to the mountain of God."],[178.17,"Is this mountain of God anywhere near where Jethro lived?"],[182.01,"What did we just read?"],[185.61,"Jethro left and go to his own land."],[187.45,"To his own land."],[188.33,"So he's not in the land where Jethro lives."],[191.49,"It's a different mountain."],[191.69,"'s a different mountain. It physical"],[199.25,"What makes a mountain the mountain of God?"],[203.41,"God's there. On top of it."],[208.35,"God manifests himself on top of it."],[212.72,"And that manifest word is important."],[214.98,"Because God's everywhere."],[217.91,"And that's one of the interesting things we're gonna see throughout the Hebrew Bible is that it's always very clear that God is everywhere."],[224.07,"But it's like, yeah, God is everywhere, but he's especially here."],[228.28,"In some particular place."],[230.92,"We've already seen that a bunch of times."],[233.34,"Remember, Jacob. wrestles with God"],[236.11,"He's going to call this place Bethel."],[238.37,"Bael, the house of God, because God is here."],[243.03,"He's not saying he's here as opposed to everywhere else, but he manifested himself there."],[250.25,"The temple is going to be the place where there's this manifestation of the glory of God."],[254.27,"So God's going to be everywhere still, but he's especially going to be there."],[258.91,"And what that means is God manifests himself there from the human perspective is if you want to go meet with God, if you want to go interact with God, that's the place you go to."],[270.19,"The place where God has chosen to manifest himself."],[273.56,"You go to meet him there."],[278.21,"And this may seem kind of abstract."],[281.81,"Here's a really practical consequence."],[284.71,"Why do you come to church instead of going and sitting on a mountain and going out into beautiful nature?"],[291.93,"God's everywhere. No one's denying that."],[298.78,"No one's denying that when you go sit on the mountain and look at nature, yes, God is there with you."],[303.5,"Absolutely. Absolutely. But where is the place where God has said he is going to manifest himself?"],[311.5,"Where free or more are gathered."],[312.99,"Yeah. That's the place."],[316.41,"And so if you're wanting to go and meet with God, you go. to the place where He said He's going to be"],[324.3,"You don't decide, well, I'm going to go where I want to go, and God can find me there."],[329.64,"It's not that He can't."],[330.84,"He certainly can."],[331.82,"Jonah found that out when he tried to run in the other direction."],[334.79,"God can come and find you."],[336.57,"No matter where you go."],[338.3,"But if you want to meet with God, if you want to draw close to God, if you want to find where God is, you go to the place where He said He's going to be."],[345.82,"That's the place you head to."],[350.44,"And so right now, that's this mountain."],[353.82,"That they just came to."],[355.9,"Before with Moses, it was another mountain, but that was still the mountain of God, because that's the place where God manifested himself."],[362.59,"In the future, it's going to be other mountains."],[364.41,"The mountain of God's going to become Mount Zion, where the temple is eventually."],[368.89,"Right down the road."],[371.05,"God is already manifesting himself in the tabernacle, for that matter."],[375.85,"The Ten of Meeting at this point."],[377.61,"It's not the tabernacle proper, we'll get to that, but the Ten of Meeting, where Moses goes to meet with them."],[385.13,"But so now he's going to manifest himself on this mountain."],[389.93,"And so I don't need to go and try and figure out which mountain this happened at, because we've got St."],[396.01,"Catherine's Monastery built on Mount Sinai."],[399.45,"That's the mountain that is currently being Mount Sinai."],[403.13,"Go and do some reading"],[404.67,"What evidence do I have for that?"],[408.19,"Moses has appeared there multiple times."],[411.31,"St. John of the Ladder, several other saints."],[416.48,"That's it right now."],[418.96,"And that's not based on me doing some material mapping or me figuring out distances here or how many days does it take to get from the Red Sea to where and where exactly did they cross the red sea?"],[430.88,"Catherine's Mount Sinai."],[432.24,"That's where it is right now."],[434.34,"That's it. Um, so yeah, so."],[438.98,"Are those manifestations?"],[440.82,"Is that what it's called Theophanies?"],[443.46,"Yeah. I mean Theophany literally means the manifestation of God."],[446.5,"So yeah I've heard the technical term, but I didn't know if it applied just to like when Jesus appears or if it's No, that could be any any manifestation of God."],[458.06,"Yeah, yeah. Um so technically, like we saw that one point on the banks of the Red Sea before God parted it, there was like multiple theophanies at once."],[468.86,"Because there's the angel of the Lord, there's the pillar, there's the voice of God speaking to Moses."],[476.34,"So the liturgy is a theophany too every week."],[480.66,"Yeah. So now notice, notice as he's talking about giving his covenant."],[488.98,"He says, if you will obey my voice and keep my covenant, then this will happen."],[490.9,"Okay Get ready for another sorry Calvinist."],[501.39,"So it is true, we're going to talk more about what a covenant is here in just a second."],[506.35,"But it is true that a covenant is something that is given."],[510.77,"God is going to give them a covenant."],[513.33,"The Hebrew the Hebrew language it's cut a covenant, but um that has to do with part of the ritual to make a covenant."],[520.61,"We talked about that with Abraham a little bit."],[522.85,"But um God is going to give them a covenant."],[526.23,"A lot of what we're gonna read for the rest of the Torah is gonna be the text, essentially, the contents of that covenant."],[533.51,"But all of the promises of that covenant."],[537.33,"He outlines them in very brief here."],[540.29,"You will be a special people to me above all nations."],[543.41,"You'll be a royal priesthood and a holy nation."],[545.9,"That's sort of a summary of the promises he's making."],[549.34,"Those are conditional upon what?"],[552.14,"Upon them keeping it, upon them listening to it."],[555.42,"Upon them keeping it, upon them being faithful to it."],[558.54,"So, yes, it's given to them as a gift, but then they have to be faithful to it to receive the blessings."],[567.02,"And there's going to be, when we get to the end of Deuteronomy, a whole bunch of curses if and when they're not faithful to it."],[574.86,"God is going to be faithful to it."],[576.42,"You don't have to worry about that."],[577.88,"But for the people to receive the blessings, they have to be faithful to it."],[582.4,"There is an if here."],[585.2,"God does not just say to Israel, you will be a holy nation and a royal priesthood."],[595.12,"He does not just say, you are a special nation to me."],[600.8,"There's an if before all of that."],[604.08,"There is an if before all of that."],[607.92,"And what that means concretely when we get to the New Testament, this is key to understanding everything St."],[614.56,"Paul is doing, is that the gospel doesn't work a different way."],[618.88,"There is an if in front of the gospel."],[622.24,"There is an if in front of eternal life, as the promise."],[628.01,"Yes, the gospel is something Jesus did."],[631.21,"It's the story of what Jesus did."],[633.61,"He died, he rose again, he ascended into heaven, rules the heavens and the earth."],[639.39,"All of that happened a couple thousand years before I was born, give or take."],[644.43,"1950, whatever. A whole long time before I was born."],[649.29,"I had nothing to do with it."],[650.89,"I didn't get him to do it."],[653.18,"I didn't do something wonderful that caused him to do it."],[656.78,"I was a sinner."],[658.24,"I was I didn't even exist, but right."],[660.04,"But But once I did exist, I was a sinner."],[663.94,"It's a gift"],[664.48,"He did it."],[667.36,"But if I want to receive the benefits, if I want to receive the blessings attached to that, I have to be faithful to it."],[676.8,"I have to be faithful to the commandments he gave."],[680.8,"When he said, if you love me, you will keep my commandments."],[686.88,"Jesus said that."],[688.0,"If you love me, you will keep my commandments."],[690.72,"We have to accept that that means the reverse is true."],[694.4,"If we don't keep his commandments, we don't really love him."],[701.0,"So New Testament doesn't present the gospel as just being you have to mentally acknowledge that this is true."],[708.6,"It doesn't present the gospel as you need to have certain feelings about this."],[715.2,"Even feelings of loyalty."],[718.96,"Feeling loyal doesn't mean anything if that loyalty doesn't manifest itself in some kind of actions."],[728.88,"And so this is the same thing."],[730.56,"But right from the beginning here, there's an if."],[735.68,"There's an if to all of the promises."],[739.68,"Now, covenant. We talked about this a little bit."],[743.04,"This covenant, the covenant at Sinai that we're talking about, follows a very particular covenant form."],[751.6,"And we'll see this."],[752.6,"We're not going to get to chapter 20 tonight, but we get into the Ten Commandments in chapter 20."],[756.76,"We're going to see kind of a perfect example of this format from the ancient world, from the late Bronze Age."],[764.12,"We have examples of it, particularly from Hittite archaeological finds."],[772.04,"Where the format that the whole book of Deuteronomy follows, that the Ten Commandments follow, that God is using here is a format that was in use at the time in the ancient Near East."],[784.06,"Because as we've talked about before, as we talked about at the beginning of Genesis especially, God is communicating to humans."],[790.78,"So he speaks to them in language they understand."],[793.5,"Both literally, like Hebrew."],[796.24,"He doesn't come and speak to them in King James English."],[799.4,"Sorry, certain folks."],[801.18,"Like he comes and speaks to them in Hebrew, a language they actually understand."],[805.31,"But not just the literal language, but the figurative language."],[810.96,"They know what an eagle is when he uses that analogy."],[815.44,"They know what he means by it."],[816.8,"They're not confused."],[817.52,"Like, wait, what's an eagle?"],[818.64,"How do you what?"],[819.52,"There wasn't a bird?"],[820.8,"What? God isn't trying to confuse them."],[823.88,"He's communicating them in language they understand."],[825.96,"And so that includes sort of the overarching format of how he communicates."],[833.16,"And so Bereet is the Hebrew word for that's translated covenant."],[838.52,"It's deathiki in Greek"],[842.32,"But a breet, um, this is a term that's used in Semitic languages to refer to this type of covenant, and it's particularly a type of covenant that was issued by a great king to vassal kings."],[859.44,"So at this time in history, individual cities are basically city states, meaning they're functioning as an independent political entity."],[868.72,"Every city has a king who's in charge."],[872.78,"But you get in certain areas, so Pharaoh is an example of this in Egypt."],[877.76,"Where he was able to project his authority over multiple cities."],[883.04,"So these are the earliest quote unquote empires"],[890.36,"So the the it really, technically speaking, there weren't empires yet."],[895.4,"Really, technically speaking, the Assyrians are the first empire, in the sense of empire taken by conquest, where there aren't middlemen between the emperor and all the areas of his rule."],[911.0,"So earlier things that are called empires, like the Hittite Empire, where we have so many examples of this, the emperor is really one of the kings of one of the cities."],[921.08,"That city rises to prominence."],[925.8,"And so that king is sort of able. to extend his will over the neighboring kings of the neighboring cities"],[933.76,"They kind of have to go with what he says because of his power influence."],[941.76,"And that could be military power, it could be economic power."],[945.45,"That they're in a position where they can control trade to these other cities."],[949.61,"So they have to kind of acknowledge his authority."],[953.29,"That could be a lot of different kinds of power."],[955.93,"Cultural production. All kinds of things can give them that power and significance."],[960.99,"So when people, to use a contemporary example, when you hear people refer to the American Empire, that's what they're really talking about."],[968.11,"So, for example, the United States of America right now, culturally, economically, can kind of extend its will into other countries."],[975.93,"The US hasn't actually gone and conquered those countries, and made them states in the United States."],[983.53,"But especially if you're saying Canada or Mexico, you you kind of have to get along with the United States if you want to have a functioning economy."],[992.47,"And trade and these kind of things."],[995.29,"So it's it's a similar kind of thing to that."],[997.71,"There's somebody who's the big dog in the yard, and so everybody kind of has to get along with the big dog so that their life will be peaceful."],[1006.03,"And so, what would happen in these situations where one sort of great king over one city could extend his authority is is that he wouldsue one of these treaties, one of these covenants."],[1018.95,"It's called a suzerain vassal treaty."],[1020.87,"The suzerain is the guy on top, the vassals are the kings underneath."],[1026.07,"And they'd be issued because he's the guy in charge."],[1028.97,"He's the one in authority."],[1030.25,"It wasn't like sometimes people will treat covenants like they're contracts."],[1034.9,"But contracts are made between like equal parties who negotiate."],[1038.84,"So if you're the big dog, you don't have to negotiate with the little dog."],[1042.78,"You could just dictate your terms, to the little dog."],[1046.4,"And so it's given from the big dog to the little dog, from the high king to the lower king."],[1052.16,"And basically is a document, a text that was structured."],[1057.36,"Of course, we're dealing with tablets at this point"],[1062.68,"At the beginning, the uh the higher king would say who he was, what he'd accomplished, how great he was, why he was the one in charge."],[1076.26,"Uh then he would, and generally what he had done in his mind for the vassal."],[1085.24,"At least in his mind."],[1086.38,"And maybe in reality."],[1088.04,"He might say, you know, I was able to defend our lands from these invaders."],[1093.26,"Whatever it is."],[1094.15,"Or I have supplied abundance of trade, you know, I have done this and that."],[1097.93,"So identify himself, what he's done for them."],[1098.89,"Now here's what I expect from you"],[1101.41,"Then lists a series of stipulations."],[1106.37,"That might be tribute."],[1107.89,"That might be, you know, if we're attacked, I expect you to send this many troops."],[1113.23,"This many people of fighting age."],[1114.85,"Whatever the terms are."],[1115.81,"This is what I expect from you."],[1117.89,"And then at the end of that, here's the good things that will happen if you meet these expectations."],[1124.82,"And then here's the bad things that will happen if you don't meet these expectations."],[1131.5,"Okay. And they would make two copies of this."],[1136.54,"So there'd be two tablets with two copies."],[1140.5,"One of them would be given to the vassal king, so he could have it there at hand and know what's expected of him."],[1147.5,"The other copy uh would be placed at the um at the feet of the idol of the vassal king's god, which was seen as calling that god to be a witness to this agreement."],[1167.99,"To help enforce if the vassal breaks it."],[1172.07,"So we'll talk, you may already be thinking, and we'll talk about this like when we get into the Ten Commandments, that follows basically that structure."],[1179.27,"The book of Deuteronomy follows basically that structure."],[1182.55,"Also, that's why there's two tablets that Moses comes down the mountain with."],[1186.39,"It's not like God couldn't fit all Ten Commandments on one."],[1186.87,"like So there was overflow onto the next one."],[1187.03,"It's two copies"],[1194.09,"But then what happens to those two copies?"],[1196.09,"The two of them get put in one place."],[1198.35,"The Ark of the Covenant, which is what?"],[1201.23,"God's footstool. There's not an idol, because God is both the king and the God."],[1207.09,"So he has both copies."],[1209.94,"So, but we'll get into more of that as we go when we get we get into that stuff."],[1213.54,"But that's the pattern."],[1214.42,"And so that's what God is setting up that He's about to do."],[1217.62,"I'm going to give you this covenant now."],[1221.23,"As your God, as your king."],[1223.41,"I'm going to give you this covenant that's going to outline what's expected of you, the good things that'll come if you meet those explanations, the bad things that will come."],[1229.17,"And that's why it's within this context of the if that we just talked about"],[1236.17,"Is he putting all of them on the level of a king, or is this just kind of the standard way it is, and so they're still like well, notice here he says that they will be what?"],[1247.53,"A royal priesthood."],[1248.73,"The royal priesthood."],[1249.77,"So he is elevated by all this way, he's elevated by de facto of this type of covenant, he's elevated them from it."],[1259.69,"Okay. That you're gonna be like priests and kings."],[1263.47,"So yes, he is."],[1264.19,"He's saying. But but so this is the last part to talk about here."],[1268.43,"Good segue. Accidental, but good segue."],[1272.99,"Um, in that notice, that the blessings he promises in the if, if you keep the commandments, if you live up to the expectations of this covenant, are relational, not absolute."],[1291.4,"And here's what I mean by that."],[1292.68,"Notice how he phrases this."],[1295.0,"If you'll obey my voice and keep my covenant, you shall be a special people to me above all nations, for all the earth is mine."],[1303.32,"Think about that a second, for as how that's rendered in English."],[1306.04,"In English, that sounds contradictory."],[1310.92,"You'll be a special nation to me because all the nations belong to me."],[1319.02,"That almost sounds contradictory."],[1323.43,"Yeah. Like contra like he's contradicting himself."],[1326.47,"Wait a minute, if they're all belong to you, then how are we special?"],[1331.8,"And this then gets further elaborated in that you shall be to me a royal priesthood in a holy nation."],[1338.52,"If they're going to be priests, if they're gonna all be priests, what does that say about their relationship to the other nations?"],[1348.44,"They have to serve life like Belo you were saying earlier."],[1351.96,"They have to bring peace and reconciliation. and all this stuff"],[1356.05,"So the blessing that's promised is you're gonna have this special priestly status. in relation to God and in relation to the other nations"],[1368.09,"And that's like what we say investors allowed."],[1373.21,"The Gentiles. Yeah, the glory of the people."],[1375.43,"So not only, as we've been talking about as we go, is Israel ethnically diverse."],[1381.53,"Originally, but Israel's specialness, its chosen status, is not just placing it above, it's not just God saying, I love you and I hate the rest of these nations."],[1396.1,"It's you've been chosen for this special role in relation to the other nations because all of them are gods."],[1403.38,"God is concerned with all of them"],[1408.88,"We've been talking about what priests do."],[1411.28,"So that means Israel should be, if they're keeping this, representing all of those nations before God and representing God before all of those nations."],[1425.25,"Well, it's interesting that this is coming right after the hierarchy within Israel."],[1430.37,"It's almost like a fractal kind of from what we just saw."],[1438.27,"Yeah. Like an individual versus like the scaling of its um which means Israel should be teaching the rest of the the nations the laws, the ordinances, command of God how to live."],[1453.27,"They should be doing it themselves, but they should be teaching the other nations."],[1456.63,"So they're not saved out of away from the nations."],[1460.76,"God's intent is to save the nations through Israel."],[1464.68,"In the same way Moses is right."],[1467.37,"And this is an important part, and St."],[1469.69,"Simeon's prayer is a window into this, but this is an important part of we've talked about how Jesus, part of him being the Christ, being the Messiah, is that he re embodies Israel."],[1482.54,"How did the nations actually end up learning God's Torah?"],[1488.86,"My ancestors. Who were out there painting themselves blue, sacrificing members of neighboring tribes to demons, dancing around fires."],[1497.86,"How did they, how did we end up in a place where I've spent, you know, decades studying the Torah?"],[1504.58,"Their descendant. Through Christ."],[1507.06,"Through Christ. Christ is the one who accomplishes this."],[1511.54,"Israel failed to accomplish this."],[1514.98,"If you read Jewish sources, well, they did kind of teach the Gentiles the Torah, and that's good"],[1528.44,"But the point is, Israel was supposed to."],[1533.56,"But they couldn't do that"],[1535.66,"Why couldn't they do that?"],[1536.62,"Well, because as we're going to read for the rest of the Hebrew Bible, for the rest of the Old Testament, they didn't keep it themselves."],[1545.18,"St. Paul brings this up explicitly in Romans."],[1550.54,"When he's talking in Romans 2, he's talking to the Jewish people."],[1553.34,"He's like, you were supposed to be the teachers of the ignorant."],[1558.06,"You were supposed to be."],[1560.19,"Those who enlightened the black."],[1561.87,"You were supposed to be teaching all of this to the Gentiles."],[1566.67,"He's talking about how the Jewish people at his time talked about oh, how horrible and corrupt and sinful and wicked the Gentiles were."],[1572.99,"were Paul says, Yeah, you supposed to do something about that."],[1573.47,"You shouldn't gloat about that"],[1580.31,"That represents your failure."],[1584.87,"To do what God do I do?"],[1587.03,"Not only did you not teach them, you became like them."],[1590.47,"You did all, you did the stuff they do."],[1593.27,"It was supposed to work the other way around."],[1595.36,"Like you were supposed to lead them out of that, not be led into it by them."],[1600.66,"And that tension we're going to see all through the rest of the Old Testament."],[1605.64,"Where Israel is going to keep becoming more and more like the other nations around them instead of the reverse."],[1612.44,"Instead of being faithful to the covenant and bringing the nations to be more like them."],[1617.88,"Set aside idolatry, set aside immorality."],[1622.02,"Set aside these things."],[1624.36,"And so uh it's important."],[1628.12,"This is not an issue of Judaism versus Christianity."],[1632.44,"This is Israel is given this by and large failed."],[1637.4,"But the Jewish Messiah, who's an Israelite, Jesus, succeeds."],[1643.81,"Accomplishes the original mission of Israel."],[1646.37,"That's why, for example, in St."],[1648.13,"John's Gospel, he says, salvation is from the Jews to a Samaritan who becomes Saint Photini and finds salvation through the Jewish Messiah, through Jesus."],[1664.13,"But so this is sort of the mission right here from the beginning"],[1671.69,"So chosen people, whenever you hear the word chosen, whether you hear it from Jewish folks about being the chosen people, whether you hear it from Calvinists about the chosen in election, the question you have to ask is chosen for what?"],[1690.25,"God doesn't just choose people in general."],[1695.1,"Doesn't choose Israel in general."],[1697.58,"He chooses Israel for something."],[1700.38,"He chooses them to do something."],[1704.14,"And there's an if attached as to whether they will do it."],[1709.94,"Same thing is true when we talk about election or being chosen in the New Testament."],[1716.98,"But God chooses people for something."],[1721.62,"To do something."],[1722.9,"And then they need to do it."],[1725.14,"They need to be faithful to it."],[1727.46,"And yes, the ones he chooses, he also calls."],[1731.86,"Calls them to do what it is he's chosen them for."],[1738.98,"But that's again when St."],[1740.82,"Paul talks about that in the New Testament, he's not making it up."],[1743.14,"He's getting it from here."],[1745.94,"He's getting it from here."],[1748.18,"And so when St."],[1749.3,"Paul says not everyone has the same calling, not everyone is chosen for the same thing."],[1754.46,"Not every nation was called to do this."],[1756.46,"Israel was called to do this."],[1760.46,"So there's this general call, for all the nations to turn from sin, to turn from the worship of idols to worshiping the true God."],[1767.82,"To put off immorality."],[1769.4,"There's this general, broad call."],[1771.16,"But then there's also a specific call to specific nations and specific people to do specific things."],[1779.08,"Paul says, whatever that call is for you, that's what you need to answer to."],[1785.96,"That's what you need to be faithful to to work out your salvation."],[1790.92,"And this enters into the church's understandings."],[1793.8,"A lot of times, especially our Protestant friends, look at a saint like St."],[1798.2,"Simeon Styleides who lived on a pillar for years."],[1802.16,"They sort of don't know what to do with that."],[1805.84,"Well, guess what?"],[1806.96,"God did not call on me to live on a pillar."],[1810.32,"Or anyone in this room, in case you were wondering."],[1813.28,"Let me sort that out for you."],[1814.64,"None of you are called to live on a pillar for years."],[1818.56,"He called Saint Simeon to go live on a pillar."],[1823.92,"That St. Simeon went and lived on a pillar, and that's how he worked out and found his salvation."],[1831.52,"And the way you and I will find and work out our salvation is by answering the call that God has given to us."],[1839.52,"Which is not going to be that."],[1842.16,"And isn't even the same for everyone in this room"],[1848.84,"But that's where we find our salvation isn't playing that role."],[1853.8,"And it's always, like in this case, it's not going to be an absolute thing."],[1857.48,"It's going to be a role."],[1858.92,"It's going to be in relation to God's people, in relation to other people."],[1866.2,"That's what God's going to be calling you to do."],[1876.92,"Okay. So Moses came and called for the elders of the people and laid before them all these words the Lord commanded him."],[1887.16,"Then all the people answered with one accord and said, Everything the Lord said we will do and hearken to."],[1893.12,"Sure. Spoilers. But they're all on board at this point."],[1898.72,"They're like, Yes, that sounds good."],[1900.56,"We'll do that."],[1902.24,"So Moses reported these words to God."],[1904.48,"The Lord then said to Moses, Behold, I come to you in the pillar of cloud, and the people may hear when I speak with you and believe you forever."],[1912.32,"So Moses reported the words of the people to the Lord."],[1916.01,"So God is saying, When I man when I speak to you, I'm going to manifest myself in this pillar of clouds, so that the people will know this is coming from me, you're not making things up."],[1927.1,"Because God knows what these folks are like."],[1929.92,"We've already seen glimpses."],[1933.08,"Again the Lord said to Moses, Go down and solemnly charge the people and sanctify them today and tomorrow, and let them wash their clothes."],[1941.08,"Let them be ready for the third day, for on the third day the Lord will descend upon Mount Sinai in the sight of all the people."],[1948.52,"You shall set bounds for the people all around, saying, Take heed to yourselves that you do not go up to the mountain or touch its base."],[1956.28,"Whoever touches the mountain shall surely die."],[1958.84,"Not a hand shall touch him, but he shall surely be stoned or shot with an arrow."],[1963.08,"Whether man or beast, he shall not live."],[1966.2,"When the thunders, the trumpets, and the cloud depart from the mountain, they shall ascend the mountain."],[1971.52,"Okay, so God says he's going to manifest himself on top of the mountain."],[1975.32,"The people need to get ready for that."],[1975.8,"need to get ready. They to meet with God"],[1980.4,"We've talked before about how God's presence is dangerous."],[1984.18,"And so we're beginning to learn it."],[1986.5,"Now there's to be much more detailed instructions coming up here in terms of moral purity and ritual purity, and we'll talk about all those in Leviticus when we get there in more detail."],[1996.02,"But we're getting the first sort of lesson of that."],[1999.48,"So we have this very obvious metaphor of be physically clean."],[2005.41,"Wash your garments, wash yourselves."],[2008.66,"That's going to help them learn about being morally clean later on."],[2014.82,"But so this is what's going to happen."],[2016.34,"You need to prepare yourselves."],[2018.74,"There's sort of a on the third day, remember, this is like what Jesus rose on the third day."],[2023.9,"This doesn't mean after three days."],[2026.38,"On the third day means there's today when I'm talking, there's gonna be a day tomorrow, and then the day after that, I'm doing it."],[2034.54,"So there's this day of preparation that's interposed here."],[2038.24,"For them to be preparing and focusing on meeting with God."],[2043.2,"And notice they're not to go near the mountain."],[2045.92,"Why? God's on top of the mountain."],[2049.04,"They don't get to run up and go see God."],[2052.5,"Because again, coming into God's presence is dangerous."],[2056.12,"Now it's not gonna, they're gonna end up being terrified."],[2058.48,"It's not gonna be a problem."],[2060.08,"But but the point being."],[2062.17,"We don't go rushing up to where God is."],[2062.81,"God comes to meet with us"],[2068.43,"It's a big part of what's going on with the iconostasis in the church."],[2072.77,"People don't all rush up to the altar to take communion."],[2077.07,"God comes out of his holy place to us and meets us where we are."],[2082.75,"So God is going to descend upon the mountain."],[2086.48,"And he is going to call certain people at certain times to come a certain amount of the way up."],[2093.45,"So that he can meet with them."],[2095.53,"So and what's the is a prohibitionist animals just kind of like a uh like a proto clean unclean thing?"],[2103.13,"Or is it just like a keep it?"],[2108.61,"It's sort of remember we talked about mentioning cattle, kind of takes it to the extreme last time."],[2115.01,"So this is not even animals."],[2118.86,"No one. Verse 14 So Moses went down from the mountain to the people and sanctified them, and they washed their clothes."],[2127.23,"Then he said to the people, be ready for the third day, do not come near your wives."],[2132.35,"Okay. So notice that isn't part of what God said to him again."],[2136.27,"It's another example, as we've said, of Moses making an application."],[2141.77,"Taking what God said and applying it."],[2144.39,"This is not your wives are dirty."],[2146.79,"Oh, they're. women, they're filthy, they're unclean"],[2149.71,"This is, you men, because he's talking to the men, because they were the ones who made these decisions in the Bronze Age."],[2157.33,"You don't need to be thinking about sex right now."],[2163.51,"You need to be focused on preparing to meet with God."],[2169.49,"And so a better translation might be leave your wives alone."],[2173.65,"Because guess what?"],[2174.53,"They do too."],[2175.73,"But this is not the time."],[2179.81,"Okay, to for you to be thinking about things like that."],[2183.22,"It's not that there's something evil or bad about that."],[2185.78,"It's we're focused on other things now."],[2186.5,"'re focused on other. We things now"],[2193.24,"Um yeah, and so this is um emblematic of how fasting in general works."],[2206.36,"Fasting isn't getting rid of things that are bad."],[2210.14,"Things that are sinful you're supposed to never do."],[2213.28,"You don't get just give up sin for lead."],[2215.2,"You're supposed to give it up totally."],[2216.5,"Like we we stop completely."],[2219.1,"Fasting of any kind is giving up something good because we're focused on and pursuing something better at a particular time."],[2230.14,"So feasting is also a good thing"],[2235.11,"We're in more of a feast period now."],[2238.12,"Where we eat the good things of the world that God has given us to enjoy."],[2242.94,"And drink the good things of the world God has given us to enjoy."],[2246.94,"And if we're married, enjoy the company of our spouses."],[2250.14,"Like all of these things are good."],[2252.48,"And it's good to it is not just good, it is important to have times of feasting."],[2259.45,"I saw some people online, so slight digression, but this irritated me."],[2264.17,"So in the Antiochian church, traditionally, we have. no fasting between Pasca and Ascension"],[2278.23,"Some other Orthodox churches, they only have no fasting during Bright Week during the first week."],[2286.31,"So I saw a bunch of people from the catechumen inquirer hive mind on the internet."],[2294.17,"Not actually Orthodox people, Orthodox adjacent people."],[2297.85,"And they're all opining and agreeing with each other about how dangerous the Antiochian practice is."],[2304.97,"How dangerous it is spiritually to go 40 days without fasting."],[2310.91,"And I thought that's probably almost as dangerous as going 50 days without feasting. like we just did"],[2323.6,"Fasting is spiritually good."],[2325.28,"Feasting, celebrating the resurrection of Christ."],[2329.13,"Celebrating the glory of God is also good."],[2332.49,"It's just as good."],[2334.49,"We need both."],[2336.35,"We need times of fasting and times of feasting."],[2339.15,"Times of warning and times of celebration."],[2341.47,"It's how life works."],[2343.6,"It's how life works."],[2346.08,"And so frankly, I think the Antiochian practice is better."],[2349.2,"Take that. Because we at least have some kind of parody between the time we spent fasting and the time we spent feasting."],[2357.44,"It's really. weird because I thought it was just gonna be like all in such yes, 40 days of feasting, but it's getting harder"],[2369.0,"Like it there is some comfort to it, you know."],[2372.04,"Yeah. I don't know."],[2373.32,"It's hard to well, yeah."],[2375.0,"I mean, there's a there's a canon in the apostolic canons that I point out to people occasionally that says that if a man refuses to uh eat meat, drink alcohol, or sleep with his wife on a feast day, uh, he is anathema."],[2391.56,"He is accursed."],[2394.52,"And do you know why it says he's accursed?"],[2397.24,"Because he has blasphemed God's creation."],[2401.88,"He has taken something that. God created and called good and called it evil"],[2409.98,"And called it bad."],[2413.6,"So traditionally, if you want to be trad."],[2417.33,"Traditionally, the church has treated feasting just as seriously as it treats fasting."],[2423.41,"I would say more seriously, because there is no canon saying you're anathema if you break a fast."],[2430.93,"You break a fast, you go to confession."],[2435.57,"You say I couldn't handle the fast, I violated it."],[2438.37,"Receive forgiveness. Whereas you're anathema."],[2442.35,"Ask Gavin Ortland how horrible that is."],[2445.49,"If you if you dare, you know, to not be with your wife on a feast day."],[2456.43,"So it that's treating feast more seriously."],[2460.13,"And the reason they treat more seriously is like the opponents of actual Christianity, like the Gnostics, like the Manicheans, like the Ankritites, all of these heretical groups."],[2474.57,"What do they have in common?"],[2476.65,"They don't feast."],[2477.85,"They don't feast."],[2480.81,"They all fast, they fast more rigorously."],[2484.89,"They physically brutalize themselves."],[2488.83,"It wasn't that they didn't fast the way Christians fast."],[2491.79,"It was that they never feast."],[2497.09,"We need to take that seriously, I think."],[2501.62,"That feasting is what separated Christianity from those heretical groups."],[2510.18,"Not that we were stricter fasters."],[2511.86,"They were way stricter on that."],[2513.14,"St. Augustine goes into the talks about how much better the Manichaeans were."],[2516.58,"If you were talking about people being pale and half dead and fasting till they were about to keel over and whipping themselves and, you know, not never sleeping."],[2527.94,"They're also straight up pagan."],[2529.78,"Well, yes. Christians"],[2530.9,"Yes, they were heathen, but the Serapians."],[2535.96,"So that's, you know, you can find, you know, if you want to talk about just brutal asceticism, Christianity's not your spot, man."],[2542.28,"You gotta there's plenty of people who have the Buddhist groups, like the Serapians, yeah."],[2546.92,"Yeah. That's way into that."],[2550.2,"Okay, let's finish up this chapter."],[2553.96,"Verse 16. So it was that on the third day in the morning, there were thunderings and lightnings and a dark cloud on Mount Sinai."],[2561.32,"Notice it's on the third day first thing in the morning."],[2565.24,"That reminds you of anything."],[2567.44,"Um a dark cloud on Mount Sinai, and the sound of the trumpet was very loud, and all the people in the camp trembled."],[2575.56,"Like I said, they're scared."],[2576.44,"'re They not gonna go bother going near the mountain."],[2582.64,"And Moses brought the people out of the camp to meet with God, and they stood at the foot of the mountain."],[2587.44,"The Mount Sinai was completely enveloped in smoke because God descended upon it in fire."],[2592.4,"Its smoke ascended like the smoke of a furnace, and the people were exceedingly amazed."],[2597.36,"There's another great translation."],[2599.52,"Wow, I am exceedingly amazed."],[2605.6,"When the blast of the trumpet sounded long and became louder and louder, Moses spoke, and God answered him by voice."],[2615.6,"Now notice this is a significant point that we've got to make"],[2620.64,"St. Gregory of Nyssa does a lot with. this in his life of Moses"],[2624.2,"Um that what's on top of the mountain is darkness."],[2632.44,"It's smoke, it's darkness."],[2634.68,"People can't see into."],[2637.0,"We tend to associate God with light."],[2643.52,"With light. But it's not, God doesn't manifest himself, even though there's fire there."],[2649.82,"Like as this blinding light on top of the mountain."],[2654.56,"We might think about Theophany."],[2656.34,"Where Christ, or not Theophany, uh, the transfiguration, where Christ is transfigured on Mount Tabor."],[2663.08,"And the light."],[2667.01,"But the blackness here, the darkness here, is what's hiding God from the people."],[2674.61,"The smoke is what's hiding God from the people."],[2677.65,"Why? Because you can't see what would happen if they saw him."],[2683.18,"So it's not that you can't see God."],[2685.42,"It's that you can't see God and live."],[2688.67,"That's the issue."],[2690.88,"So he is in darkness to protect them."],[2695.84,"And so this is important when we put that up against the transfiguration."],[2702.32,"The transfiguration. When St."],[2706.08,"Paul, for example, says there's one mediator between God and man and Christ Jesus, it talks about Christ's flesh."],[2707.04,"'s He not just speaking abstractly or in terms of a role that Jesus has."],[2723.8,"Meaning the veil of the temple that stood there to protect the people from God's holiness."],[2743.64,"Now they still freak out, as you can see in the icon."],[2746.12,"So one of my favorite things of that icon is I think it's St."],[2748.6,"James has his sandal flying off."],[2751.18,"Because they're all ah."],[2752.86,"Um, but they're able to survive it."],[2757.24,"They're able to look upon the glory of God and the face of Jesus Christ, which they couldn't see here."],[2765.96,"Because it would kill them, it would destroy them."],[2770.84,"So that that juxtaposition is intentional on top of those two mountains."],[2776.04,"And remember, Moses ends up showing up at both of them."],[2779.29,"On top of the mountain at both of them."],[2785.29,"Verse 20. Then the Lord came down upon Mount Sinai on the top of the mountain, and the Lord called Moses to the top of the mountain, and Moses went up."],[2793.85,"Then God spoke to Moses, Go down and solemnly charge the people, lest they break through to gaze at God and many of them perish."],[2801.86,"They don't need to be running up here because they'll die."],[2806.15,"Also let the priests who come near the Lord God sanctify themselves, lest he destroy some of them."],[2812.47,"So they're going to be offering sacrifices at the base of the mountain."],[2817.19,"So before they come to do that, they need to sanctify themselves."],[2823.35,"But Moses said to God, The people cannot come up to Mount Sinai, for you solemnly charged us, saying, Set bounds around the mountain and sanctify it."],[2831.35,"The Lord then said to him, Go, go down and then come up, you and Aaron with you."],[2835.99,"But do not let the priests and the people break through to come up to God, lest the Lord destroy some of them."],[2844.27,"So notice something here."],[2848.11,"Notice the language."],[2859.55,"Not let the priests of people break through to come up to God, lest Yahweh destroy some of them."],[2869.71,"Why is God referring to himself in the third person?"],[2873.47,"Jesus. Second person"],[2875.55,"So there's someone who is Yahweh, who is God, who Moses is talking to."],[2880.03,"Standing there talking to."],[2883.35,"And who says to him, Don't let the people come up here, because if they do, Yahweh, God, will destroy some of them."],[2898.16,"So this is yet another place."],[2899.6,"We've seen a bunch of these already, where there's these two figures."],[2905.74,"There's a voice, and only a voice, that calls Moses up there, and then there's someone he's standing there talking to."],[2915.42,"A finer point is going to be put on this later, but it's already introduced here."],[2918.78,"We already see this distinction being made."],[2922.78,"Verse 25 So Moses went down to the people and spoke to them."],[2932.02,"So he goes down and again reminds them hey, stay away from the bottom of the mountain."],[2939.54,"You will die."],[2940.42,"God doesn't want you to die."],[2943.3,"But that will be the result of you disobeying and trying to come up here and pry into what God is doing."],[2952.9,"So I think we went a little long tonight, so we'll wrap up relatively quickly."],[2956.74,"But uh next week, when we come back, we'll get into chapter 20 and the Ten Commandments, and there'll probably a few things to say about the Ten Commandments, I imagine."],[2964.42,"So thank you, everybody."],[2968.1,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study. of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God"],[2975.42,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2980.78,"That's wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":21.6,"lv":2,"h":"19:1-6 - Sinai: eagles' wings and the offer","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>3rd month</b> after leaving Egypt → camped before the mountain, <b>Sinai</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Moses up; God: \"you have seen what I did… how I bore you on <b>eagle's wings</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"This is <b>not literal</b>… not Lord of the Rings\" - eagles did not carry them</li><li class=\"d1\">maybe where Tolkien got it - \"ask Father Andrew\"; obviously <b>figurative</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>If</b> you obey my voice, keep my covenant → <b>special people</b> above all nations</li><li class=\"d1\">\"all the earth is mine\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Royal priesthood</b> and <b>holy nation</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Third item on his list of things that <b>don't interest him</b></li><li class=\"d1\">already: <b>age of the earth</b>, <b>date of the Exodus</b>; now <b>location of Mount Sinai</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"endless journal articles\"</li></ul>"},{"t":115.84,"lv":3,"h":"Which mountain? Where God manifests","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Notice: this \"mountain of God\" is <b>not near where Jethro lived</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Jethro left to <b>his own land</b> → different mountain from Moses' first</li><li class=\"d0\">What makes it the mountain of God? <b>God manifests himself on top of it</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"manifest\" is key - God is <b>everywhere</b>, but <b>especially here</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Jacob → <b>Bethel</b>, house of God; later the <b>temple</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Human consequence: to meet God, <b>go where he said he'd be</b></li><li class=\"d1\">why come to <b>church</b> instead of sitting on a mountain in nature?</li><li class=\"d1\">\"where two or three are gathered\"; God can find you anywhere (<b>Jonah</b>)</li><li class=\"d0\">Mountain shifts: this one → later <b>Mount Zion</b>; <b>Tent of Meeting</b> already</li><li class=\"d0\">Don't need to map it: <b>St. Catherine's Monastery</b> = Mount Sinai now</li><li class=\"d1\">evidence: <b>Moses appeared there</b> multiple times; <b>St. John of the Ladder</b>, other saints</li></ul>"},{"t":438.98,"lv":3,"h":"Q: theophanies","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: are these manifestations called <b>theophanies</b>?</li><li class=\"d1\"><i>theophany</i> literally = <b>manifestation of God</b>; not only when Jesus appears</li><li class=\"d0\">Red Sea: <b>multiple theophanies at once</b></li><li class=\"d1\">angel of the Lord, the pillar, the voice speaking to Moses</li><li class=\"d0\">\"The <b>liturgy is a theophany</b> too every week\"</li></ul>"},{"t":480.66,"lv":2,"h":"The covenant is a gift - with an \"if\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"If you obey my voice and keep my covenant\" - \"sorry Calvinists\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Covenant is <b>given</b> by God (Hebrew: \"<b>cut</b> a covenant\" = ritual, cf. Abraham)</li><li class=\"d1\">rest of the Torah = <b>contents of the covenant</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Promises summarized: <b>special people</b>, <b>royal priesthood</b>, <b>holy nation</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>conditional</b> on keeping it, being faithful</li><li class=\"d1\">end of <b>Deuteronomy</b>: curses if unfaithful; \"God is going to be faithful\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>\"There is an if\"</b> before all of it → key to understanding <b>St. Paul</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Gospel</b> isn't different: an if before <b>eternal life</b></li><li class=\"d1\">gospel = what Jesus did; I had nothing to do with it - <b>a gift</b></li><li class=\"d1\">but to receive blessings → <b>be faithful to his commandments</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"If you love me, you will keep my commandments\" → reverse: don't keep them, <b>don't love him</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not just mental assent or feelings, even <b>loyalty</b> - must show in <b>actions</b></li></ul>"},{"t":739.68,"lv":2,"h":"Covenant form: suzerain-vassal treaty","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Sinai covenant follows a <b>particular covenant form</b> - perfect example in ch. 20</li><li class=\"d1\">late Bronze Age; <b>Hittite</b> archaeological finds; also <b>Deuteronomy</b> and the Ten Commandments</li><li class=\"d0\">God speaks in language they understand - <b>literal</b> (Hebrew, \"not King James English\") and <b>figurative</b> (eagle)</li><li class=\"d0\"><i>berit</i> = covenant (Greek <i>diatheke</i>); issued by a <b>great king to vassal kings</b></li><li class=\"d1\">city-states; one king projects authority - Pharaoh</li><li class=\"d1\">first true <b>empire by conquest</b> = <b>Assyrians</b>; Hittite \"empire\" = one city's king rises by military, economic, cultural power</li><li class=\"d1\">today's \"American Empire\" - Canada, Mexico \"have to get along\" with the <b>big dog in the yard</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Suzerain</b> = top; <b>vassals</b> = kings beneath</li><li class=\"d1\">not a <b>contract</b> - equals negotiate; the big dog <b>dictates terms</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1052.16,"lv":2,"h":"Structure of the treaty and the two tablets","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Text on <b>tablets</b>, structured:</li><li class=\"d1\">1. who he is, what he's done, why he's in charge (\"I defended your lands\")</li><li class=\"d1\">2. <b>stipulations</b> - tribute, troops, \"this is what I expect\"</li><li class=\"d1\">3. <b>blessings</b> if kept; 4. <b>curses</b> if broken</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Two copies</b>: one to the vassal; one at the <b>feet of the vassal's god's idol</b> → god as <b>witness</b>/enforcer</li><li class=\"d0\">Ten Commandments and Deuteronomy follow this pattern</li><li class=\"d1\">why <b>two tablets</b> - not overflow, <b>two copies</b></li><li class=\"d1\">both placed in the <b>Ark = God's footstool</b>; no idol since God is <b>both king and god</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Setting up: \"my God, your king\" - what's expected, good things, bad things - all inside the <b>if</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1236.17,"lv":3,"h":"Q: royal priesthood","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: is he putting all of them on the level of a king?</li><li class=\"d1\">yes - \"<b>royal priesthood</b>\" → elevated by this type of covenant</li><li class=\"d1\">\"priests and kings\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1268.43,"lv":2,"h":"Blessings are relational, not absolute","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Blessings of the if are <b>relational</b>, not absolute</li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Special</b> people to me above all nations, <b>for all the earth is mine</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">sounds <b>contradictory</b> in English - if all are his, how are we special?</li><li class=\"d0\">Answer: <b>royal priesthood</b> → <b>special priestly status</b> toward God and toward the other nations</li><li class=\"d1\">they \"serve\" the nations - bring <b>peace and reconciliation</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Israel was <b>ethnically diverse</b> from the start</li><li class=\"d0\">Chosen status isn't \"I love you, hate the rest\"</li><li class=\"d1\">chosen for a <b>role</b> - God is concerned with <b>all</b> the nations</li></ul>"},{"t":1408.88,"lv":2,"h":"Priests represent nations before God","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">What priests do → Israel <b>represents the nations before God</b> and <b>God before the nations</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Comment: right after the hierarchy within Israel - \"<b>fractal</b>\", individual vs scaling up</li><li class=\"d0\">Should <b>teach the nations</b> God's laws, ordinances, commands - and keep them themselves</li><li class=\"d1\">\"not saved <b>out of</b> the nations\" → God's intent is to <b>save the nations through Israel</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>St. Simeon's prayer</b> a window into this</li><li class=\"d0\">Part of Jesus being <b>Messiah</b>: he <b>re-embodies Israel</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1482.54,"lv":3,"h":"How the nations learned Torah: through Christ","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"How did the nations <b>actually</b> learn God's Torah?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">his ancestors \"painting themselves blue, sacrificing neighbors to demons, dancing around fires\"</li><li class=\"d1\">now decades studying Torah → <b>through Christ</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Christ accomplishes</b> what Israel failed to</li><li class=\"d1\">Jewish sources: they did teach Gentiles somewhat - but supposed to</li><li class=\"d0\">Why failed: <b>didn't keep it themselves</b> - rest of the OT</li></ul>"},{"t":1545.18,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 2: Israel became like the nations","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>St. Paul, Romans 2</b>: \"teachers of the ignorant… enlightened the blind\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Jews gloating at how wicked the Gentiles were → Paul: <b>that's your failure</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not only didn't teach them - <b>became like them</b></li><li class=\"d1\">supposed to lead them out, not be led in</li><li class=\"d0\">Tension through the OT: Israel more like the nations, <b>idolatry, immorality</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Not Judaism vs Christianity</b>: Israel by and large failed; the <b>Jewish Messiah</b> succeeds</li><li class=\"d1\">John's Gospel: \"<b>salvation is from the Jews</b>\" - to a Samaritan who becomes <b>St. Photini</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1671.69,"lv":2,"h":"\"Chosen\" - chosen for what?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Chosen\" - Jewish chosen people, <b>Calvinist election</b> → ask: <b>chosen for what?</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God doesn't choose people <b>in general</b> - chooses them <b>to do something</b></li><li class=\"d1\">an <b>if</b> attached; same for election in the NT</li><li class=\"d0\">Those he chooses he also <b>calls</b> - to what he chose them for</li><li class=\"d1\">Paul in the NT is \"getting it from <b>here</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>General call</b> to all nations: turn from sin, idols, immorality</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Specific call</b> to specific people to specific things</li><li class=\"d1\">\"whatever that call is for you, answer to it\" → <b>work out your salvation</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1790.92,"lv":2,"h":"Simeon Stylites: your own calling","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Protestant friends don't know what to do with <b>St. Simeon Stylites</b>, on a pillar for years</li><li class=\"d1\">\"God did not call <b>me</b> to live on a pillar… none of you\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>he</b> found salvation that way</li><li class=\"d0\">You and I → <b>answering the call God gave us</b> - \"not going to be that\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not even the same for everyone in the room</li><li class=\"d0\">Never absolute - a <b>role in relation to God's people</b>, other people</li></ul>"},{"t":1876.92,"lv":2,"h":"19:7-13 - The people agree; prepare for the third day","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Moses calls elders; people: \"<b>Everything the Lord said we will do</b>\" - \"Spoilers\"</li><li class=\"d0\">God: I come in the <b>pillar of cloud</b> so people hear and <b>believe you forever</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"he knows what these folks are like\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Sanctify</b> them today and tomorrow; <b>wash clothes</b>; ready for the <b>third day</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Lord descends on Sinai <b>in sight of all the people</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Bounds</b> around the mountain - touch it → <b>die</b>, stoned or shot with an arrow, man or beast</li><li class=\"d0\">When trumpet and cloud depart → they may ascend</li></ul>"},{"t":1980.4,"lv":3,"h":"God's presence is dangerous","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>God's presence is dangerous</b> - first lesson; detail in <b>Leviticus</b> (moral and ritual purity)</li><li class=\"d0\">Obvious metaphor: <b>physically clean</b> → later <b>morally clean</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"On the third day\" - like Jesus rose</li><li class=\"d1\">not \"after three days\": today, tomorrow, then <b>the day after</b></li><li class=\"d1\">day of <b>preparation</b> focused on meeting God</li><li class=\"d0\">Don't go near - \"God comes to meet with us\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>iconostasis</b>: people don't rush the altar; God comes out of his holy place to us</li><li class=\"d0\">He calls certain people at certain times <b>part of the way up</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2095.53,"lv":2,"h":"Q: animals and verse 14","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: ban on animals - proto clean/unclean?</li><li class=\"d1\">\"mentioning cattle takes it to the extreme\" - <b>no one</b>, not even animals</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>19:14-15</b>: \"do not come near your wives\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>not</b> in what God said → <b>Moses applying</b> God's word</li><li class=\"d1\">not \"women are dirty\" - speaking to the men</li><li class=\"d1\">\"you don't need to be thinking about sex right now\" → focus on <b>meeting God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">better: <b>leave your wives alone</b> - they have to prepare too</li><li class=\"d1\">nothing evil about it - \"focused on other things now\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2193.24,"lv":3,"h":"Fasting gives up good things","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Emblematic of how fasting works</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not giving up bad things - sin you give up <b>totally</b></li><li class=\"d1\">fasting = giving up something <b>good</b> for something <b>better</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Feasting</b> is good too - good things of the world, <b>spouses</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not just good, <b>important</b> to have times of feasting</li></ul>"},{"t":2259.45,"lv":2,"h":"Digression: Pascha to Ascension","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Antiochian: <b>no fasting between Pascha and Ascension</b>; others only Bright Week</li><li class=\"d1\">online \"catechumen inquirer hive mind\" - \"how <b>dangerous</b> to go 40 days without fasting\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"as dangerous as <b>50 days without feasting</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Need <b>both</b> - fasting and feasting, \"warning and celebration\" → \"how life works\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Antiochian practice is better\" - <b>parity</b> between fasting and feasting time</li><li class=\"d0\">Comment: feasting 40 days is hard - comfort in the fast</li></ul>"},{"t":2375.0,"lv":3,"h":"Apostolic canon on feasting; heretics don't feast","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Apostolic canon</b>: refuses meat, wine, or <b>sleeping with his wife</b> on a feast day → <b>anathema</b></li><li class=\"d1\">because he <b>blasphemed God's creation</b> - called good evil</li><li class=\"d0\">Church treats feasting <b>more seriously</b> than fasting</li><li class=\"d1\">break a fast → <b>confession</b>; no canon anathematizing</li><li class=\"d0\">Gnostics, Manicheans, Encratites - what in common? <b>They don't feast</b></li><li class=\"d1\">fasted <b>more rigorously</b>, brutalized themselves</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>feasting</b> separated Christianity, not stricter fasting</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Augustine</b>: Manichaeans pale, half dead, whipping themselves</li><li class=\"d0\">Want brutal asceticism? \"Christianity's not your spot\" - Buddhist groups</li></ul>"},{"t":2550.2,"lv":2,"h":"19:16-19 - Thunder, trumpet, smoke","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Third day, first thing in the morning</b> - reminds you of something</li><li class=\"d0\">Thunder, lightning, <b>dark cloud</b>, very loud trumpet → camp <b>trembled</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Moses brings people out to the <b>foot of the mountain</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Sinai <b>enveloped in smoke</b> - God descended in <b>fire</b>, smoke like a furnace</li><li class=\"d1\">\"exceedingly amazed\" - \"Wow\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Trumpet louder and louder; Moses speaks, <b>God answers by voice</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2615.6,"lv":2,"h":"Darkness on the mountain vs Tabor","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>St. Gregory of Nyssa</b>, <i>Life of Moses</i>: on top is <b>darkness</b>, smoke</li><li class=\"d1\">we associate God with <b>light</b> - not a blinding light here, though fire</li><li class=\"d0\">Compare <b>transfiguration, Mount Tabor</b> - light</li><li class=\"d1\">darkness <b>hides God from the people</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not that you can't see God - \"<b>can't see God and live</b>\" → darkness protects them</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>One mediator</b> between God and man (Paul) → Christ's <b>flesh</b></li><li class=\"d1\">like the <b>veil of the temple</b> protecting from God's holiness</li><li class=\"d0\">Apostles still freak out - James' <b>sandal flying off</b> in the icon</li><li class=\"d1\">but survive seeing <b>the face of Jesus Christ</b> - couldn't here</li><li class=\"d0\">Juxtaposition <b>intentional</b>; <b>Moses on both mountains</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2785.29,"lv":2,"h":"19:20-25 - Moses called up; Yahweh and Yahweh","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Lord comes down; <b>calls Moses to the top</b>; Moses goes up</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Go down and charge the people <b>lest they break through to gaze</b> and perish\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Priests</b> must sanctify themselves - will offer <b>sacrifices at the base</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Moses: people can't come up, you told us to set bounds</li><li class=\"d0\">Lord: go down, come up <b>with Aaron</b>; not priests and people - \"lest the Lord destroy some of them\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2859.55,"lv":3,"h":"Two figures: God speaks of Yahweh in the third person","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Why does God refer to himself in the <b>third person</b>? (not second: \"Jesus\")</li><li class=\"d1\">someone <b>who is Yahweh</b> talking to Moses says \"<b>Yahweh</b> will destroy\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Two figures</b>, as seen already</li><li class=\"d1\">a <b>voice only</b> calls Moses up; then <b>someone he stands talking to</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Finer point put on this later\" - distinction already introduced</li></ul>"},{"t":2922.78,"lv":3,"h":"19:25 and wrap-up","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Moses goes down, tells them <b>stay away</b> from the mountain</li><li class=\"d1\">\"God doesn't want you to die\" - result of disobeying and trying to <b>pry into what God is doing</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Ran long - wrapping up</li></ul>"}],"next":"Next week: <b>Exodus 20</b> - the <b>Ten Commandments</b>"});
